<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="ws-1">
  <title>Worksheet 1: Sections 1.1, 1.2, 2.1 - Review of Functions, Rates of Change, Secant and Tangent Lines</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>For reference as you go:</p>
    <ol marker="a)">
      <li>
        <p>
          The worksheet has two pages and includes six problems, some of which, labeled with (<alert>AP</alert>), are intended as additional practice outside of class.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          The point-slope equation of a line with slope <m>m</m> passing through the point <m>(x_1,y_1)</m> is given by
          <me>y-y_1 = m(x-x_1).</me>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Completing the square:
          <md>
            <mrow>ax^2+bx+c \amp = a(x+k)^2+h,</mrow>
            <mrow>\text{where} \qquad k \amp = \frac{b}{2a} \qquad \text{and} \qquad h = c-\frac{b^2}{4a}.</mrow>
          </md>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Absolute value function:
          <me>
            f(x)=|x|=\begin{cases}
            x \amp \text{if } x \geq 0 \\
            -x \amp \text{if } x \lt 0
            \end{cases}
          </me>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Some algebraic identities:
          <md>
            <mrow>a^2-b^2 \amp = (a-b)(a+b)</mrow>
            <mrow>(a-b)(a+b) \amp = a^2-b^2</mrow>
          </md>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </introduction>

  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>Find the domain and range of each of the following functions:</p>
      <ol marker="(a)" cols="2">
        <li><p>(<alert>AP</alert>) <m>f(x)=x^3+3</m></p></li>
        <li><p><m>g(x)=x^2 - 6x + 5</m></p></li>
        <li><p>(<alert>AP</alert>) <m>h(x)=2\sqrt{x+1}+1</m></p></li>
        <li><p><m>k(x)=|x-2|-3</m></p></li>
        <li><p>(<alert>AP</alert>) <m>l(x)=-2\cos(x-\pi)</m></p></li>
        <li><p><m>m(x)=\dfrac{\sin^2(2x)}{2}</m></p></li>
        <li><p><m>y=\dfrac{2-x}{|3x-6|}</m></p></li>
        <li><p>(<alert>AP</alert>) <m>y=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt[4]{t}}</m></p></li>
        <li><p>(<alert>AP</alert>) <m>y=\ln(s-5)</m></p></li>
        <li><p><m>y= -e^s+2</m></p></li>
      </ol>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Suppose that <m>f(x)=\sqrt{2x-1}</m> and <m>g(x)=x^2+1</m>. Find <m>(f\circ g)(x)</m>, <m>(g \circ f)(x)</m>, and their domains.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        For each of the following functions and intervals, find the difference quotient
        <me>\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}.</me>
      </p>
      <ol marker="(a)">
        <li>
          <p><m>f(x) = \ln(x)+5</m> on <m>[1,9]</m>. Simplify your answer, if possible.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>(<alert>AP</alert>) <m>g(x) = 4x^2-e^x</m> on <m>[x,a]</m>, where <m>a \gt x</m>. <em>(Note: No need to simplify your answer)</em></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><m>k(x) = \sqrt{x-4}</m> on <m>[x,x+h]</m>, where <m>h \gt 0</m>. <em>(Note: No need to simplify your answer)</em></p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        You may use Desmos to recall the graph of <m>f(x)=\dfrac{1}{x}</m>. Using what you know about reflecting, shifting, and stretching, match the transformations of <m>f(x)</m> shown below with their equations.
      </p>
      <ol marker="(a)" cols="3">
        <li><p><m>y=\dfrac{-3}{x}</m></p></li>
        <li><p><m>y=\dfrac{1}{x+1}-1</m></p></li>
        <li><p><m>y=2\left(\dfrac{1}{x+1}+1\right)</m></p></li>
      </ol>
      <figure>
        <caption>Transformations of <m>f(x) = \frac{1}{x}</m></caption>
        <image source="WS1.PNG" width="40%">
          <shortdescription>Graphs of three rational functions representing transformations of 1/x.</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </figure>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        The graph of a function <m>f(x)</m> is shown in the figure. By inspecting the graph, fill in the bubble next to the correct ordering of the quantities <m>A</m> through <m>E</m>.
      </p>
      <sidebyside widths="60% 35%" valign="top">
        <stack>
          <ol marker="A.">
            <li><p>The slope of the tangent line to the graph of <m>f(x)</m> at <m>x=1</m></p></li>
            <li><p>The slope of the secant line between <m>x=0</m> and <m>x=1</m></p></li>
            <li><p>The instantaneous rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> at <m>x=-2</m></p></li>
            <li><p>The average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> over the interval <m>[-1,2]</m></p></li>
            <li><p><m>\dfrac{f(2)-f(-2)}{4}</m></p></li>
          </ol>
          <p><em>Answer:</em></p>
        </stack>
        <image source="fa24quiz1pic1.png">
          <shortdescription>Graph of a cubic function f(x) used to compare tangent and secant slopes.</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </sidebyside>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find the equation of the secant line through the points on <m>g(x)=e^{x-1}-x-1</m> where <m>x=1</m> and <m>x=2</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>